    "created_at": "2020-09-22T23:04:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-09-22T23:04:13Z",
    "body": "> Sysinfo has been very slow in the memory_usage module on windows (#1564).\r\n\r\nThank you for the heads up; I will keep it in mind. Hopefully the issue is restricted to memory measurements.\r\n\r\n> I'd be happy to submit a PR for this once GuillaumeGomez/sysinfo#363 is fixed.\r\n\r\nNow that the `sysinfo` issue has been fixed and a new version released, it would be a good time to discuss the design of a possible storage module.\r\n\r\nFirstly: is it a storage module, or strictly a disk usage module? Sysinfo doesn't e.g. provide information on USB-attached storage, and it would be wise to start with what we have at hand. @SarthakSingh31 suggests that a foremost concern is noticing when space runs low, which seems sensible.\r\n\r\n> `💾 (<drive mount point | drive name | empty>: <used percentage | free percentage>%) | (another drive)`\r\n> Example:\r\n> `💾 sda1: 60% | sda2: 20%` or just `💾 60%` and `💾 20%` depending on the drive the user is in.\r\n\r\nOne thing to note is that Starship's default prompt is already on the busy side. Columns mount up quickly once you start adding names or mount points.",
